    {
      "category": "fibre",
      "label": "Fibre & Textile Making",
      "description": "The places that put on a day of wool: mills with working looms, shops that sell a ticket as well as yarn, and the heritage projects that have taken a fibre strand and run with it.\nShort on purpose. Munster has plenty of craft venues and almost none of them are about fibre — a gallery with a textile show twice a decade is not a source, it is a coincidence. The first version of this catalogue was full of arts centres and craft fairs; they are gone, and what is left is the handful of places where wool is actually the subject.\nBuilt county by county from a sweep of the Heritage Week programme, on the reasoning that whoever ran a fibre day in August runs them the rest of the year too. That is how Clonmel, Bunratty and Kilfenora got here. **Waterford is still missing**, and it is not for want of looking: nothing in the sweep, no guild branch, no mill.",
      "sourceCount": 6,
      "eventCount": 0
    },
    {
      "category": "guilds",
      "label": "Guilds & Networks",
      "description": "The bodies whose whole purpose is this subject: the weavers', spinners' and dyers' guild, the textile networks, the wool council.\nThese matter more than venues here. A one-off fibre day in Munster is usually organised by two people in a guild rather than programmed by a building, and a guild's news page is the closest thing to a diary the subject has. They are also where a visiting tutor gets announced — which is exactly how a Shetland knitting weekend ends up on an island off Cork.",
      "sourceCount": 4,
      "eventCount": 1
    },
    {
      "category": "notices",
      "label": "Listings & Notices",
      "description": "The nets: national schemes with searchable programmes, the craft agencies, and the two West Cork papers that covered the flax revival when nobody else did.\nA one-off run by two people has no website, so this is where it gets written down — but nearly everything these sources carry is out of scope. They are fetched for the textile strand and nothing else.",
      "sourceCount": 7,
      "eventCount": 0
    }
  ],
